From a951d6b31b54b4cd1cb8b1ad17ae222621791a1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snarayana <snarayana@student.ethz.ch>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:39:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix: keep sglang 0.5.20's JIT caches
 (SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR and the rest)

sglang 0.5.20 moved load_jit's build cache from TVM_FFI_CACHE_DIR to
SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR (python/sglang/kernels/jit/utils/compile/cache.py:302),
which defaults to ~/.cache/sglang/jit and does not follow SGLANG_CACHE_DIR.
servekit set only TRITON_CACHE_DIR, TVM_FFI_CACHE_DIR and
FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE, so on 0.5.20 the custom all-reduce kernels built
during torch.distributed init (17 s of 19.5 s at TP4 in the 0.5.16 A/B) went
into the job's ephemeral $HOME and were rebuilt on every launch.

CACHES now lists every variable that moves a compile cache in sglang 0.5.16
and 0.5.20 and the kernel libraries they ship with, and all of them are set
every time: a version that does not read one ignores it.

tests/test_jit_cache.py resolves, per release, every location the engine
compiles into and checks it lands under servekit's root;
tests/test_jit_cache_regression.py reproduces the miss end to end and fails
on cd8f0b8.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
